1
00:00:00,349 --> 00:00:05,461
The Week Planner — Plan your hours ahead — and see how they compare with the time you actually report.

2
00:00:06,588 --> 00:00:12,192
The Week Planner is one of WorkDesk's tabs. Let's open it from the tab bar at the top.

3
00:00:15,526 --> 00:00:21,644
Each column is one day. Today is outlined in orange, and the blocks you have planned sit on their day.

4
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:28,467
The top of each day shows two numbers: the hours you planned (p) and the hours you actually reported (a).

5
00:00:29,093 --> 00:00:35,971
Up here are the totals for the period: Planned, Actual, the Variance between them, and your Capacity — the hours in your contract.

6
00:00:36,646 --> 00:00:41,511
To plan time, click + plan on the day you want. Let's plan Tuesday morning.

7
00:00:44,442 --> 00:00:50,565
A planned entry opens. Set the start and the end — the number of hours is worked out for you.

8
00:00:54,878 --> 00:01:01,481
Choose the hour type: Yellow for client work, Red for company time — and Blue for management, if your role has it.

9
00:01:03,677 --> 00:01:08,558
Then pick the client and the project. The project list only shows that client's projects.

10
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:18,601
If you like, tie it to a work order and to one of your Taskana tasks — or leave them empty.

11
00:01:20,753 --> 00:01:24,868
Add a short description, so you remember what the time is for.

12
00:01:29,802 --> 00:01:36,908
Remember: a plan is only a plan. Planned entries don't count as reported hours — you still report your time in the Time Log.

13
00:01:37,594 --> 00:01:41,012
Click Save, and the block appears on Tuesday.

14
00:01:44,029 --> 00:01:48,135
Here it is. The totals at the top have been updated too.

15
00:01:48,822 --> 00:01:53,444
Click a block to change any of its details — or to delete it.

16
00:01:56,279 --> 00:02:00,632
Delete is at the bottom left. We'll keep this one, so let's cancel.

17
00:02:03,326 --> 00:02:07,679
Plans change. To move a block to another day, just drag it there.

18
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:15,261
It moved to Wednesday.

19
00:02:16,146 --> 00:02:20,502
Your open Taskana tasks that have a due date are suggested up here.

20
00:02:21,249 --> 00:02:23,752
Drag one onto a day…

21
00:02:27,586 --> 00:02:34,257
…and the planner fills in the client, the project, the task and the description for you. Just set the hours and save.

22
00:02:37,124 --> 00:02:42,497
Team leads and managers can plan for their team as well. Choose the person under Planning for.

23
00:02:44,469 --> 00:02:48,824
Now you see Eitan's week. When you change someone's plan, they are notified.

24
00:02:51,093 --> 00:02:58,213
Happy with this week? Copy week puts every block into next week too — a quick start for a week that looks the same.

25
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:05,548
Use the arrows to move between weeks. Here's next week — already planned.

26
00:03:08,941 --> 00:03:12,344
This week always brings you back to today.

27
00:03:15,092 --> 00:03:18,974
Switch between a Day, a Week and a four-week Month view.

28
00:03:27,086 --> 00:03:33,188
And Export downloads the plan next to the actual hours as an Excel workbook — handy for a weekly review.

29
00:03:33,853 --> 00:03:40,727
If a week is planned past your contracted hours, an orange warning tells you — so you can spread the work in time.

30
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:46,565
Plan · compare · adjust — Plan ahead, report as you go, and see the difference. More help: the Handbook → Week Planner.
